PKGBUILD_MODEL(3)

# NAME

pkgbuild_model - native package-build values and identity domains

# DESCRIPTION

A *materialized_source* binds one source declaration to observed SHA-256 bytes.
The observed digest must equal the digest carried by the sealed source snapshot.

A *resolved_package_input* binds one exact build or check package subject to a
concrete package release, source snapshot, upstream build result, and artifact.
A *materialized_package_input* additionally binds the filesystem-tree identity
made available to execution.

An *environment_policy* is closed and typed. Version 1 fixes C.UTF-8, UTC,
denied network access, and an isolated home. Parallelism, umask, and optional
SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH are sealed. Ambient name/value maps are not authority.

A *payload_manifest* is an ordered complete set of canonical package objects.
It retains path, type, mode, numeric ownership, size, timestamp, regular-content
digest, symbolic-link target, hard-link topology, and device numbers.

A *sealed_artifact* records encoding, compression, exact byte count, and SHA-256.
Its pathname is not part of the value.

All identities use domain-separated canonical SHA-256 records.

# SEE ALSO

*libpkgbuild*(3), *pkgbuild_request*(3), *pkgbuild_result*(3)
